    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense looks primed for a productive day, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, who anchor the lineup with elite efficiency scores of 81.88 and 75.27, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park boost and faces V\u00e1squez, whose 4.89 xERA offers a high ceiling for run production from the two-hole. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** catches a favorable matchup against Gibson (5.87 xERA) in a hitter-friendly environment, making both players essential for our 5x5 targets today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a high-value play at 71.33; his 14% platoon edge against Castillo is a primary driver in his elevated status, providing a necessary boost to our AVG and SB floor.\n\nWhile our starters are set, the bench decision surrounding **Nolan Schanuel** was the most difficult. **Nolan Schanuel** posted a respectable 44.14, but he ultimately fell short of the starting rotation due to a projected efficiency deficit compared to the middle infield and utility group. We also closely evaluated **Miguel Vargas**, who remains a high-upside asset, but his matchup against a difficult arm like Yamamoto depressed his score to 41.93, keeping him on the bench. Conversely, **Sam Antonacci** remains in the lineup despite a tough matchup against Yamamoto; while his score of 48.56 is lower than ideal, his position at leadoff and his underlying xwOBA suggest he is the best available option to chase R and SB volume despite the SP skill disadvantage.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding **Liam Hicks** and **Wade Meckler**, who are hovering near the marginal tier with scores of 54.07 and 41.07. **Wade Meckler** is particularly thin given the matchup against Jax, though he holds his spot to preserve our daily roster flexibility. Meanwhile, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** remains a void in our outfield production, but we are effectively managing the rotation with the depth provided by **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, who provide steady scoring floors today against Burke. We will monitor the weather reports for any late-breaking wind shifts that could further impact the park factors for the afternoon slate.",
